<title>USA: NIKE earns $177 million, sales up 55 percent.</title>
<headline>NIKE earns $177 million, sales up 55 percent.</headline>
<dateline>BEAVERTON, Ore. 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>NIKE, Inc. said Wednesday its profits leaped 80 percent in its second quarter to $176.9 million, up from $97.8 million a year earlier, as sales jumped by 55 percent.</p>
<p>The maker of athletic footwear and apparel said sales totaled $2.10 billion, up from $1.36 billion a year earlier, and orders for the period from December 1996 through April 1997 totaled $4.1 billion, up 54 percent from the year-earlier pace.</p>
</text>
